A Circular Queue is a queue where the last position connects back to the first position.
Instead of wasting space like a normal queue, we reuse empty positions.

Normal Queue Problem:

[10 20 30 40 50]
Dequeue twice →

[ _ _ 30 40 50 ]
Rear cannot move further → space wasted

Circular Queue Solution:
Use modulo:

rear = (rear + 1) % k
